    '["Put the corn flour in a bowl and add the salted water little by little, mixing with the flour until all the water has been used and the flour has become a dough.","Let it rest for five minutes.","Now, shape the dough into round rolls about 3 inches in diameter and 1/2 inch thick.","In a lightly greased skillet, slowly cook the arepas until a crust forms on each side.","Now place them into a casserole and bake in the oven at 350 degrees for approximately 20 minutes, until the arepas sound hollow when tapped.","To enhance taste: instead of using just water, use chicken or beef broth."]'::jsonb,
