    '["Prepare the Figs","Cut off the hard bits of stalk and then cut the figs in half length ways.","Place the figs in a small frying pan / saute pan with the cut side face up and add the water around them.","Leave the figs on a medium heat to cook through, once they become soft remove them from the pan and place onto a serving dish.","This will take around 10 - 15 minutes.","Prepare the Syrup","In the pan there will be a red water juice left from the figs.","Add the sugar while remaining on a medium heat.","Stir continuously for a couple of minutes until the juice has turned to a thick syrup.","Remove from the heat.","Push one half of walnut into every fig and then drizzle the syrup over the top.","Serve warm or cooled."]'::jsonb,
