    '[{"name":"Flour","amount":"250g","category":"grains"},{"name":"Butter","amount":"125g","category":"dairy"},{"name":"Egg","amount":"1","category":"dairy"},{"name":"Salt","amount":"Pinch","category":"spices"},{"name":"Cheese","amount":"300g","category":"dairy"},{"name":"Milk","amount":"100ml milk","category":"dairy"},{"name":"Eggs","amount":"3","category":"other"},{"name":"Parmesan Cheese","amount":"100g","category":"dairy"},{"name":"Plum tomatoes","amount":"350g","category":"other"},{"name":"White Vinegar","amount":"3tbsp","category":"condiments"},{"name":"Honey","amount":"1 tbsp","category":"other"},{"name":"Basil","amount":"Topping","category":"spices"}]'::jsonb,
    '["Crust: make a dough from 250g flour (I like mixing different flours like plain and wholegrain spelt flour), 125g butter, 1 egg and a pinch of salt, press it into a tart form and place it in the fridge.","Filling: stir 300g cream cheese and 100ml milk until smooth, add in 3 eggs, 100g grated parmesan cheese and season with salt, pepper and nutmeg.","Take the crust out of the fridge and prick the bottom with a fork.","Pour in the filling and bake at 175 degrees C for about 25 minutes.","Cover the tart with some aluminium foil after half the time.","In the mean time, slice about 350g mini tomatoes.","In a small pan heat 3tbsp olive oil, 3tbsp white vinegar, 1 tbsp honey, salt and pepper and combine well.","Pour over the tomato slices and mix well.","With a spoon, place the tomato slices on the tart, avoiding too much liquid on it.","Decorate with basil leaves and enjoy"]'::jsonb,
