    '["Place the corn, water, chicken or vegetable bouillon, garlic, salt, pepper, cilantro, potatoes and scallions in a large pot and bring to a boil.","Reduce heat to medium low and simmer for approximately 4 minutes or until the corn is tender.","Remove from the heat.","Puruée the soup in a blender and return to the pot, add the cream and heat over medium heat for 15 minutes, stirring occasionally.","Pour into bowls, garnish with cilantro and potato sticks.","*Fresh corn or frozen corn will work for this soup recipe.","I usually use fresh corn, but I use organic corn kernels in the winter to make this soup.","*To store: Place cooled corn soup in an airtight container and store in the fridge for up to 3 days."]'::jsonb,
