    '["Make the Dough: Mix flour and salt in a large bowl.","Add butter, using your fingers to blend into a crumbly texture.","Gradually add water, mixing until a dough forms.","Wrap and chill for 30 minutes.","Prepare the Filling: Cook onions in a pan until translucent.","Add ground beef, cooking until browned.","Stir in spices, then remove from heat.","Once cooled, mix in eggs and olives.","Assemble: Roll out the dough and cut into circles.","Place a spoonful of filling in each, fold over, and seal the edges.","Cook: Bake at 200°C (400°F) for 20-25 minutes, or until golden.","Pro Tips:","For a flakier crust, incorporate a tablespoon of vinegar into the dough mixture.","This helps prevent gluten formation.","Seal the edges of the empanadas with a fork to ensure they do not open during baking or frying."]'::jsonb,
