    '["Sift flour, baking powder, salt, and sugar together.","In a separate bowl, beat 6 eggs, then blend in the butter and milk.","Sprinkle one tablespoon of sev dzandig (black seeds) and all the mahleb on top of the dry ingredients.","Make a hole in the center of the dry ingredients and pour the wet ingredients in all at once, mixing with a few strokes until the dough can be turned out onto a floured board.","Add more flour if necessary; it shouldn''t be too sticky.","Knead the mixture gently, just a few times, and then roll it out until it is ½\" thick.","Cut it into diamond shapes, circles, or long strips which can be rolled and braided into loaves.","Prick each piece several times with a fork.","Beat the seventh egg with additional sev dzandig (black seeds) added.","Brush each piece of koulenje with this glaze and place on cookie sheet covered with baking parchment.","Bake at 400° for 12-15 minutes until slightly golden.","Cool on a rack.","These are best eaten warm.","You can reheat them by wrapping in foil."]'::jsonb,
