    '["Preparation","In a mixing bowl mix together the summer squash, sugar, eggs and baking soda.","Add the flour and continue to mix, you are looking for a thick sticky mixture.","Add a bit more flour if the mixture is still thin and slightly runny.","In a large round baking tray (about 2 inches deep) rub some olive oil over the base and edges.","Scoop the mixture onto the tray and spread out evenly, then pour a small amount of olive oil onto you hand and rub it in circles gently over the top of the mixture.","This should flatten it and leave it with a slightly shiny glossing.","Bake in the oven for 40 minutes on 180 degrees – the top should be a golden brown once cooked.","Leave to cool before slicing into squares and serving."]'::jsonb,
