    '[{"name":"Dried Shrimp","amount":"50g","category":"meat"},{"name":"Rice","amount":"40g","category":"grains"},{"name":"Coconut","amount":"100g","category":"other"},{"name":"Orange Zest","amount":"20g","category":"fruit"},{"name":"Chilli","amount":"3","category":"other"},{"name":"Peanuts","amount":"50g","category":"other"},{"name":"Pickled Scallion Heads","amount":"100g","category":"other"},{"name":"Pickled Scallion Head Brine","amount":"30 ml","category":"other"},{"name":"Galangal","amount":"25g","category":"other"},{"name":"Shallots","amount":"30g","category":"other"},{"name":"Orange Juice","amount":"20 ml","category":"fruit"},{"name":"Lime juice","amount":"50 ml","category":"fruit"},{"name":"Fish Sauce","amount":"50 ml","category":"meat"},{"name":"Palm Sugar","amount":"50g","category":"other"}]'::jsonb,
    '["Rinse the rice, soak in water for about 10 minutes, then drain well.","Heat a wok or large skillet over medium heat.","Add the rice and stir constantly until evenly dark golden brown and very fragrant, about 5 minutes.","Transfer to a bowl to cool.","Grind finely using a spice grinder or mortar and pestle, then sift through a fine mesh strainer to remove any large pieces.","Set aside.","Thinly slice the shallots lengthwise.","Finely chop the galangal, pickled scallion heads, chili peppers, and bitter orange zest.","Coarsely grind the roasted peanuts.","Heat a frying pan over low heat, add shredded coconut, and toast, stirring, for 2–3 minutes.","Set aside.","In a large bowl, combine lime juice, bitter orange juice, palm sugar, pickled scallion brine, and fish sauce.","Stir until fully dissolved and well mixed.","In a mixing bowl, combine dried shrimp, toasted coconut, chopped aromatics, and dressing.","Mix well.","Add roasted rice powder and stir again.","Top with coarsely ground roasted peanuts.","Place the salad on a large plate.","Let each guest spoon a little onto their own small plate, wrap in leafy greens with vegetables, and enjoy in bite-size portions.","For a vegetarian version, omit the dried shrimp and fish sauce.","Season to taste with soy sauce and a pinch of sea salt, keeping the sweet-sour balance."]'::jsonb,
