    '[{"name":"Ground Pork","amount":"1 lb","category":"meat"},{"name":"Coconut Milk","amount":"1 cup","category":"dairy"},{"name":"Prahok","amount":"3  tablespoons","category":"other"},{"name":"Vegetable Oil","amount":"2 tablespoons","category":"condiments"},{"name":"Garlic","amount":"4 Cloves Crushed","category":"vegetables"},{"name":"Shallots","amount":"2 chopped","category":"other"},{"name":"Chilli","amount":"2","category":"other"},{"name":"Brown Sugar","amount":"1 tablespoon","category":"other"},{"name":"Fish Sauce","amount":"2 tablespoons","category":"meat"},{"name":"Lime","amount":"Juice of 1","category":"fruit"},{"name":"Cilantro","amount":"Garnish","category":"other"}]'::jsonb,
    '["Heat 2 tbsp vegetable oil in a large skillet over medium-high heat until shimmering, about 1 minute.","Add 4 cloves minced garlic and 2 finely chopped shallots to the skillet, stirring constantly until fragrant and lightly golden, 2-3 minutes.","Tip: Keep the heat medium to prevent burning—garlic can turn bitter if overcooked.","Add 1 lb ground pork to the skillet, breaking it up with a spoon, and cook until no pink remains, 5-7 minutes.","Stir in 3 tbsp prahok and cook for 1 minute to blend the flavors, mashing it slightly into the pork.","Pour in 1 cup coconut milk, stirring to combine, then reduce heat to medium-low and simmer for 10 minutes until the mixture thickens slightly.","Tip: Simmer gently to avoid curdling the coconut milk—a steady bubble is ideal.","Add 2 tbsp fish sauce, 1 tbsp palm sugar, and 2 minced Thai chilies, stirring until the sugar dissolves, about 2 minutes.","Remove the skillet from heat and stir in 2 tbsp lime juice, mixing thoroughly.","Tip: Add lime juice off the heat to preserve its fresh, tangy flavor without cooking it out.","Transfer the dip to a serving bowl and garnish with ¼ cup chopped fresh cilantro.","Let the dip cool for 5 minutes before serving to allow the flavors to meld."]'::jsonb,
