    28,
    false,
    '[{"name":"Vegetable Oil","amount":"1 tablespoon","category":"condiments"},{"name":"Chicken Thighs","amount":"1 lb","category":"meat"},{"name":"Onion","amount":"1 medium chopped","category":"vegetables"},{"name":"Garlic","amount":"3 Cloves Crushed","category":"vegetables"},{"name":"Ginger","amount":"1 tablespoon","category":"other"},{"name":"Red Curry Paste","amount":"2 tablespoons","category":"other"},{"name":"Coconut Milk","amount":"1 can","category":"dairy"},{"name":"Chicken Stock","amount":"1 cup","category":"meat"},{"name":"Fish Sauce","amount":"1 tablespoon","category":"meat"},{"name":"Brown Sugar","amount":"1 tablespoon","category":"other"},{"name":"Bamboo Shoot","amount":"1 cup","category":"other"},{"name":"Red Pepper","amount":"1 sliced","category":"spices"},{"name":"Basil","amount":"Pinch","category":"spices"},{"name":"Lime","amount":"To serve","category":"fruit"}]'::jsonb,
    '["Heat 1 tbsp vegetable oil in a large pot or Dutch oven over medium-high heat until it shimmers, about 2 minutes.","Add 1 lb chicken pieces to the pot and cook until browned on all sides, approximately 5–7 minutes, stirring occasionally to prevent sticking.","Remove the chicken from the pot and set it aside on a plate, leaving any oil and juices in the pot.","Reduce the heat to medium and add 1 sliced onion to the pot, cooking until softened and translucent, about 4 minutes.","Stir in 3 cloves minced garlic and 1 tbsp grated ginger, cooking for 1 minute until fragrant to avoid burning.","Add 2 tbsp red curry paste to the pot and cook for 1 minute, stirring constantly to toast the spices and deepen the flavor.","Pour in 1 can coconut milk and 1 cup chicken broth, scraping the bottom of the pot to incorporate any browned bits for extra richness.","Stir in 1 tbsp fish sauce and 1 tbsp palm sugar until fully dissolved, then return the browned chicken to the pot.","Bring the mixture to a gentle boil, then reduce the heat to low, cover, and simmer for 15 minutes to allow the flavors to meld.","Add 1 cup bamboo shoots and 1 sliced red bell pepper to the pot, simmering uncovered for an additional 5 minutes until the vegetables are tender-crisp.","Remove the pot from the heat and stir in 1 cup Thai basil leaves until just wilted, about 1 minute, to preserve their fresh aroma.","Serve the curry hot, garnished with lime wedges for a bright, acidic finish."]'::jsonb,
