    '[{"name":"Silken Tofu","amount":"16 ounces","category":"other"},{"name":"Soy Sauce","amount":"3  tablespoons","category":"condiments"},{"name":"Chinese Sesame Sauce","amount":"2 tablespoons","category":"condiments"},{"name":"Scallions","amount":"1 sliced","category":"other"},{"name":"Sesame Seed","amount":"2 tsp","category":"other"}]'::jsonb,
    '["Prepare the tofu:","Drain the tofu and gently remove it from its packaging onto a large plate.","Carefully slice the tofu into 1/2-inch slabs widthwise.","With the palm of your hands, gently push the sliced tofu sidewise so that they fan out over the plate.","Garnish with toppings and serve:","Drizzle the soy sauce and sesame sauce on top.","Then garnish it with scallions and sesame seeds, and serve.","Tightly cover leftovers and refrigerate for up to 2 days.","You can enjoy it cold straight out of the fridge or you can reheat it by microwaving in 30-second increments until warmed through"]'::jsonb,
