    '["Soak herring in cold water for at least 1 hour.","If very salty, repeat, changing the water each time.","Drain thoroughly and slice herring into bite-size pieces.","Place in a jar large enough to accommodate the pieces and cover with oil, allspice, peppercorns, and bay leaf.","Close the jar.","Refrigerate for 2 to 3 days before eating.","This will keep refrigerated up to 2 weeks.","Serve with finely chopped onion or onion slices, lemon, and parsley or dill."]'::jsonb,
