    '[{"name":"Brown Sugar","amount":"2 cups","category":"other"},{"name":"Butter","amount":"¼ cup","category":"dairy"},{"name":"Eggs","amount":"2","category":"other"},{"name":"Vanilla Extract","amount":"1 tsp","category":"other"},{"name":"Salt","amount":"1 tsp","category":"spices"},{"name":"Plain Flour","amount":"½ cup","category":"grains"},{"name":"Milk","amount":"1 1/2 cups","category":"dairy"}]'::jsonb,
    '["Preheat oven to 350 degrees F (175 degrees C).","Grease a 9-inch pie dish.","Place the brown sugar and butter in a mixing bowl, and beat them together with an electric mixer until creamy and very well combined, without lumps.","Beat in eggs, one at a time, incorporating the first egg before adding the next one.","Add the vanilla extract and salt; beat the flour in, a little at a time, and then the milk, making a creamy batter.","Pour the batter into the prepared pie dish.","Bake in the preheated oven for 35 minutes; remove pie, and cover the rim with aluminum foil to prevent burning.","Return to oven, and bake until the middle sets and the top forms a crusty layer, about 15 more minutes.","Let the pie cool to room temperature, then refrigerate for at least 1 hour before serving."]'::jsonb,
