    '["Boil some water in a large saucepan.","Add 250ml cold water and the udon noodles. (As they are so thick, adding cold water helps them to cook a little bit slower so the middle cooks through).","If using frozen or fresh noodles, cook for 2 mins or until al dente; dried will take longer, about 5-6 mins.","Drain and leave in the colander.","Heat 1 tbsp of the oil, add the onion and cabbage and sauté for 5 mins until softened.","Add the mushrooms and some spring onions, and sauté for 1 more min.","Pour in the remaining sesame oil and the noodles.","If using cold noodles, let them heat through before adding the ingredients for the sauce – otherwise tip in straight away and keep stir-frying until sticky and piping hot.","Sprinkle with the remaining spring onions."]'::jsonb,
